 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 550743,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>The following is a food web for a meadow habitat that occupies 25.6 km<sup>2</sup>. The primary producers’ biomass is uniformly distributed throughout the habitat and totals 1,500 kg/km<sup>2</sup>. Developers have approved a project that will permanently reduce the primary producers’ biomass by 50 percent and remove all rabbits and deer. Which of the following is the most likely result at the completion of the project?</p>\n\n<p><img src=\"exercises/media/c42e1ef804e1d4e5.jpg\" alt=\"A food web begins with meadow grasses, which are eaten by deer, rabbit and vole. Deer and rabbit are eaten by coyote. Rabbit and vole are eaten by hawk.\"></p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1082600,
     "content_html": "The biomass of coyotes will be 6 kg, and the biomass of hawks will be 0.5 kg."
    },
    {
     "id": 1082601,
     "content_html": "The biomass of coyotes will be dramatically reduced."
    },
    {
     "id": 1082602,
     "content_html": "The coyotes will switch prey preferences and outcompete the hawks."
    },
    {
     "id": 1082603,
     "content_html": "There will be 50 percent fewer voles and 90 percent fewer hawks."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
